    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d805">

                <pb facs="0882" n="596" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2356</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 18, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.50 a. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s form letter 300.115/6886 to parcel-post claimants. Department’s
                    understanding that innocent mail may go forward immediately erroneous.
                    Procurator General in official ruling states:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>Goods seized in parcels mail will not be released if shipment infringes any
                        British orders in council unless shipment made under arrangement with His
                        Majesty’s Government. Although certain classes of goods with enemy
                        destination and goods of enemy origin with neutral destination are not
                        contraband, it is none the less the intention of Procurator General to
                        proceed against them under appropriate order in council.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
